<h1>ISSUE-83: Use of the dt and dd elements in figure and details content models</h1>
<h2>dt-dd-semantics</h2>
<h2>Use of the dt and dd elements in figure and details content models</h2>
<dl>
<dt>State:</dt>
<dd>CLOSED</dd>
<dt>Product:</dt>
<dd><a href='/html/wg/tracker/products/1'>HTML 5 spec</a></dd>
<dt>Raised by:</dt>
<dd><a href='/html/wg/tracker/users/'>Michael[tm] Smith</a></dd>
<dt>Opened on:</dt>
<dd>2009-09-29</dd>
<dt>Description:</dt>
<dd>The content models for the &lt;figure&gt; and &lt;details&gt; elements use the &lt;dt&gt; and &lt;dd&gt; elements, but give them different semantics.<br />
<br />
Related bugs:<br />
<a href="https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=7657">http://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=7657</a><br />
<a href="https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=7669">http://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=7669</a><br />
<br />
Issue 83 <a href="/html/wg/tracker/actions/152">ACTION-152</a> dt/dd Change Proposal by Shelley Powers, November 10, 2009<br />
<br />
At burningbird:<br />
<a href="https://burningbird.net/node/82">http://burningbird.net/node/82</a><br />
<br />
Also in the ESW Wiki:<br />
<a href='http://esw.w3.org/topic/HTML/ChangeProposals/DdDt'>http://esw.w3.org/topic/HTML/ChangeProposals/DdDt</a> </dd>
